# 37. AI Agent Implementation Rules

The coding agent must follow these rules.

### Rule 1

Do not implement cryptography from scratch.

### Rule 2

Do not store plaintext files on the backend.

### Rule 3

Do not store master encryption keys in PostgreSQL.

### Rule 4

Do not make blockchain transactions part of ordinary file upload.

### Rule 5

Do not require port forwarding for users.

### Rule 6

Do not require users to configure servers manually.

### Rule 7

Every upload must be resumable.

### Rule 8

Every encrypted object must be integrity-verifiable.

### Rule 9

Every critical operation must be idempotent.

### Rule 10

Never delete the only copy of a file before another verified copy exists.

