## Final product principle

The system should make the following statement true:

> **"Your phone takes the photo. Your personal devices store it. The network backs it up. Encryption protects it. Recovery protects you from losing access. Blockchain can provide ownership and economic coordination—but the user never needs to understand any of it."**

The first implementation should therefore **not start with blockchain or decentralized storage**. Start with the **encrypted sync + personal storage node + 2-of-3 recovery protocol**. Those three components establish the core product. Decentralized storage and blockchain can then be added behind stable interfaces without redesigning the application.
